ote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1649_53872_1354511"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A reserved portion of memory used to temporarily store data, pending an instruction to complete its transfer to or from a file.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="53872">file buffer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1354511">بفر فایل</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16495_592342_2299316"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A number that identifies a certain Internet application. For example, the default port number for the WWW service is 80.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592342">port number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299316">نمبر درگاه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16496_592343_1990263"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An apartment that consists of exactly one thread.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592343">single-threaded apartment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1990263">اپارتمان یک رشته ای</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16496_592344_1990263"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An apartment that consists of exactly one thread.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592344">STA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1990263">اپارتمان یک رشته ای</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="165_127792_2531268"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In computer graphics, a line drawn in a certain direction from a starting point to an endpoint, both of whose locations are identified by the computer using x-y-coordinates on a grid. Vectors are used in the output of some graphics programs instead of groups of dots (on paper) or pixels (on screen).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="127792">vector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2531268">بردار</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16504_592353_1897632"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart that shows a three dimensional surface that connects a set of data points. As in a topographic map, colors and patterns indicate areas that are in the same range of values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592353">surface chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897632">گراف سطحی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16505_592354_2765890"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to a resource in a failover cluster or server cluster that is in the process of being brought online or offline.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592354">pending</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2765890">معوقه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16506_592355_1897633"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A surface chart subtype that provides a view of the surface chart from above, with colors representing specific ranges of values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592355">contour chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897633">گراف حد فاصل</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16507_592356_1897634"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A contour chart displayed without color.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592356">wireframe contour chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897634">گراف نواری بی رنگ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16508_2909978_1897635"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart that displays data in rings, where each ring represents a data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2909978">donut</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897635">گراف حلقوی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16508_592357_1897635"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart that displays data in rings, where each ring represents a data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592357">doughnut chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897635">گراف حلقوی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16511_592360_1897636"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A doughnut chart that displays the contribution of each value to a total while emphasizing individual values, by showing each slice of the doughnut as "pulled out," or separate, from the whole.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592360">exploded doughnut chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897636">گراف حلقوی باز شده</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16513_592362_2299199"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A best-fit curved trendline that is used when the rate of change in the data increases or decreases quickly and then levels out.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592362">logarithmic trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299199">خط گراف لوگاریتمی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16514_592363_1897637"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A curved trendline that is used when data fluctuates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592363">polynomial trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897637">خط گراف چند جمله ای</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16516_592365_1897638"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A curved trendline that is used with data sets that compare measurements that increase at a specific rate.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592365">power trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897638">خط گراف توانی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16518_592368_2299112"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A curved trendline that is used when data values rise or fall at constantly increasing rates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592368">exponential trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299112">خط گراف لوگاریتمی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16519_592369_1897639"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A trendline that smoothes out fluctuations in data to show a pattern or trend more clearly.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592369">moving average trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897639">خط گراف اوسط متحرک</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16525_592375_2701068"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user whose account resides in an account partner organization and who can access federated applications that reside in a resource partner organization. In the context of Office 365, a federated user is one that is sourced (mastered, authenticated, created, and managed) in an organization’s on-premises Active Directory. The on-premises Active Directory has a trust relationship with the cloud that allows authenticated Active Directory users to access cloud resources (or “services,” such a SharePoint Online, Exchange Online, etc).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592375">federated user</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2701068">استفاده کننده یکجا شده</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16533_592383_2299470"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A certificate that represents the public-key portion of a token-signing certificate. A verification certificate is stored in the trust policy and used by the federation server in one organization to verify that incoming security tokens have been issued by valid federation servers in the organization's farm and in other organizations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592383">verification certificate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299470">تصدیق تأیید</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16543_592397_2701055"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">For BitLocker Drive Encryption, a combination of one or more of the following elements, identified by a globally unique identifier (GUID): personal identification number (PIN), recovery password, recovery key, startup key, and Trusted Platform Module (TPM).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592397">authentication method</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2701055">شیوه موثق سازی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16577_592433_1506163"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To ensure that all data sources that are used by a KPI or scorecard are available.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592433">validate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506163">معتبر کردن</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1658_115875_2299404"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of running a management agent that imports data from a connected data source into the connector space, and then immediately stopping the run.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="115875">staging</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299404">مرحله بندی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16584_592444_2592171"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A directory name, used in an address, that corresponds to a physical directory on the server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592444">virtual directory</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2592171">دایرکتوری مجازی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16594_592578_2194565"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service or feature that renders the audio content of a television or video program as text on the screen. These captions are usually visible only if decoded or activated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592578">closed captioning</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2194565">نشر معلومات زیرنویس در صفحه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16607_592811_1499541"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A numeric or other designation appended to a product name to identify a particular release.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592811">version</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1499541">نسخه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16609_592813_1506164"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An effect applied to a graphical object that typically reduces the difference between the outline of the object and the graphical area next to it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592813">blur</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506164">خیره</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16612_592816_2299392"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A wireless, mobile device that combines platform software, a browser, a modern chipset, and a telephone handset.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592816">smartphone</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299392">تلیفون هوشمند</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16612_592837_2299392"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A wireless, mobile device that combines platform software, a browser, a modern chipset, and a telephone handset.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592837">phone</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299392">تلیفون هوشمند</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16647_594141_1990255"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Software that provides encryption for sensitive data, such as passwords, in applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="594141">encryption provider</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1990255">ارائه کنندۀ رمزگذاری</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16658_600620_1897640"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The round button in the lower left-hand corner of the Windows screen that allows the user to click and display the Start menu.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="600620">Start button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897640">دکمۀ آغاز</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16665_601385_2626226"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An attack by a malicious user or malicious software on a computer or operating system to find a secret password or a symmetric encryption key by guessing passwords or keys until the correct password or key is discovered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="601385">key search attack</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626226">حمله نیروی بی رحم</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16665_601385_2626230"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An attack by a malicious user or malicious software on a computer or operating system to find a secret password or a symmetric encryption key by guessing passwords or keys until the correct password or key is discovered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="601385">key search attack</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626230">حمله کلید جستجو</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16665_601386_2626226"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An attack by a malicious user or malicious software on a computer or operating system to find a secret password or a symmetric encryption key by guessing passwords or keys until the correct password or key is discovered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="601386">brute force attack</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626226">حمله نیروی بی رحم</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16665_601386_2626230"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An attack by a malicious user or malicious software on a computer or operating system to find a secret password or a symmetric encryption key by guessing passwords or keys until the correct password or key is discovered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="601386">brute force attack</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626230">حمله کلید جستجو</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1668_147156_1499297"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A grouping of properties presented as a tabbed page of a property sheet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="147156">property page</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1499297">صفحۀ خصوصیت</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16697_601660_1698074"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft site that provides a comprehensive listing of updates that can be distributed over a corporate network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="601660">Microsoft Update Catalog</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1698074">فهرست Microsoft Update</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1679_1370400_1946073"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The W3C standard language used for writing XML schema documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1370400">XSD</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1946073">XML schema</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1679_1536620_1946073"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The W3C standard language used for writing XML schema documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1536620">XML schema definition language</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1946073">XML schema</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1679_1536621_1946073"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The W3C standard language used for writing XML schema documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1536621">XSDL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1946073">XML schema</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1679_257436_1946073"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The W3C standard language used for writing XML schema documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="257436">XML schema</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1946073">XML schema</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16798_616805_1897641"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft implementation of an integrity level. In particular, a protection level, refers to an integrity label that contains only level information, without the additional information traditionally contained within integrity level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="616805">protection level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897641">سطح محافظتی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1682_114990_1897224"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An array (arrangement of items) in which many of the entries are identical, commonly zero. It is not possible to define precisely when an array is sparse, but it is clear that at some point, usually when about one-third of the array consists of identical entries, it becomes worthwhile to redefine the array.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="114990">sparse array</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897224">آرایۀ پراگنده</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1686_90627_1354672"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A distinct chunk of text that is indicated by formatting such as indentation, numbering, or a new line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="90627">paragraph</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1354672">پاراگراف</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1688_74871_1499117"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In word processing, a string of characters displayed or printed in a single horizontal row.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="74871">line</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1499117">خط</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16907_627846_1506165"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The date when a project or task is scheduled to begin.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="627846">begin date</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506165">تاریخ آغاز</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16907_627847_1506165"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The date when a project or task is scheduled to begin.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="627847">start date</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506165">تاریخ آغاز</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16924_629472_2299035"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The name automatically assigned to an object by a program or process when the user does not specify an alternative.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629472">default name</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299035">اسم حالت اصلی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16927_629486_2299043"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user-defined description of a particular device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629486">device name</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299043">اسم دستگاه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1695_397155_2299098"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hidden item that contains information about an event sink, information about what events will trigger the event sink, and options that tell when or under what conditions the event sink will be triggered. The event registration item is created in the same folder that is being monitored for events.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397155">event registration item</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299098">فقره راجستر کردن رویداد</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16957_629941_2299004"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A dialog box in which a user confirms that he or she wants a specified action to occur, usually by clicking OK.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629941">confirmation dialog box</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299004">جعبه دایلوگ تأیید</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16960_629944_2299078"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A three-digit string of numbers, such as 5.1.2., that indicates the status of an attempt to deliver an email message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629944">DSN code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299078">کود DNS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16962_629946_2299082"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The value that is applied to a specific DWORD.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629946">DWORD value</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2299082">مقدار DWORD</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16963_629993_1953839"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique view for displaying appointments, tasks, and other information in the form of a Web page. You can customize the Outlook Today page for your organization, or for individuals or groups within your organization, to display the information most relevant to them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629993">Outlook Today</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1953839">Outlook امروز</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16983_636758_1897642"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The search engine that enables users to search data from disparate sources across an organization. It is a shared service that provides extensive and extensible content gathering, indexing, and querying. This service supports full-text searching using a Structured Query Language (SQL)-based query syntax, and provides a keyword syntax to support keyword searches.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="636758">Enterprise Search</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1897642">جستجوی سازمانی</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="170_502935_1498662"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A part of the user interface dedicated to a particular purpose, such as "instant message area."</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="502935">area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1498662">ناحیه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1700_122674_1499515"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of viewing and updating the actual progress of tasks so that you can see progress across time, evaluate slippage of tasks, compare scheduled or baseline data to actual data, and check the completion percentage of tasks and your project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="122674">tracking</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1499515">دنبا ل کردن</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17003_637212_1354446"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The user account that the worker processes servicing the application pool use as their process identity. Process identity is the term that is used to denote the account that a process runs under.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="637212">application pool identity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1354446">شناسنامۀ محل برنامه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17004_1262414_1354662"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An XML file with the .config file name extension that contains settings for an application, Web site, or server. Common configuration files include Machine.config and Web.config.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1262414">configuration file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1354662">فایل تنظیم بندی .وب</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17004_637213_1354662"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An XML file with the .config file name extension that contains settings for an application, Web site, or server. Common configuration files include Machine.config and Web.config.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="637213">Web.config file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="prs-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1354662">فایل تنظیم بندی .وب</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNo